    "name": "Private Service Connect — GCP",
    "story": "Serverless compute runs in the Databricks-managed serverless plane, outside the customer's VPC. To reach a private target on-premises, the customer builds a chain in the hub VPC: a Hybrid Connectivity NEG holding the target's private IP and port, an internal TCP Proxy Load Balancer using that NEG as its backend (its Envoy proxies run in a regional proxy-only subnet advertised to on-prem over BGP), and a Private Service Connect service attachment in front of the load balancer's forwarding rule, using a dedicated PSC NAT subnet. A private endpoint rule in the workspace's NCC connects serverless to that service attachment. Traffic then reaches the data centre over Cloud Interconnect or HA VPN. The workspace VPC is peered to the hub and is not on the serverless path. The customer owns and maintains the load balancer chain; use it when a Private Network Gateway is not an option.",
